posts.body:
Nirriti said:
So when youve got the drop on the enemies, you get a free escape?
Click to expand...
Yes, as long as you use it immediately. If you wait until the next turn, it's not free anymore.
Nirriti said:
That said, during their escape, they stay facing the enemies
(instead of turning around)
and dont run either. Their sprites remain static and move backward!
Click to expand...
Hmm. Maybe something like this could work…? I haven't tested. Put it in a .js file and add it as a plugin near the bottom of the list.
JavaScript:
(function(old) {
    Sprite_Actor.prototype.retreat = function() {
        old.call(this);
        this.scale.x = -1;
    };
})(Sprite_Actor.prototype.retreat);

Try using that plugin and the escape item common event has:
Script:
$gameParty.performEscape();
SoundManager.playEscape();
BattleManager._escaped = true;
Wait: 60 frames
Script:
BattleManager.processAbort();
Or you can change the plugin a bit to increase the retreat move time:
Sprite_Actor.prototype.retreat = function() {
this.scale.x = -1;
this.startMove(300, 0, 60);
};
PS. Just to make sure, the rpg maker mz character generator has the same frame for escape for all frames I think, so unless you've changed the escape frames, you'll see it "frozen", even if the motion is looping by default.
